%N A399865 Number of preclosures on an n-element labeled set; equivalently, number of extensive order-preserving self-maps of the Boolean lattice of rank n.
%C A399865 Terminology is not uniform: Burris requires only extensivity and isotonicity, whereas Claes and Sonck additionally require c({})={}. A Čech preclosure operator also preserves binary unions. For each x in S, the sets A contained in S\{x} for which x is in c(A) form an upset of the Boolean lattice P(S\{x}). Conversely, any choice of one such upset for each x in S determines a preclosure. There are M(n-1) choices for each x, independently, where M(k) is the k-th Dedekind number A000372(k).
%D A399865 G. Birkhoff, Lattice Theory, 3rd ed., American Mathematical Society Colloquium Publications, Vol. 25, 1967, p. 63.
%D A399865 Donald E. Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming, Vol. 4A, Section 7.1.1, p. 79.
%H A399865 S. N. Burris, <a href="https://shareok.org/bitstreams/6790f577-b39a-4efe-9980-a4aeeb19879d/download">Theory of Pre-Closures</a>, Ph.D. dissertation, University of Oklahoma, 1968.
%H A399865 V. Claes and G. Sonck, <a href="https://doi.org/10.4995/agt.2003.2006">The quasitopos hull of the construct of closure spaces</a>, Appl. Gen. Topol., vol. 4, no. 1, pp. 15-24, Apr. 2003. See Definition 2.2.
%H A399865 D. J. Kleitman and G. Markowsky, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1975-0382107-0">On Dedekind's problem: The number of isotone Boolean functions. II</a>, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 213 (1975), 373-390.
%F A399865 a(0) = 1; a(n) = A000372(n-1)^n for n >= 1.
%Y A399865 Cf. A000372 (Dedekind numbers), A014466 (Dedekind numbers minus 1), A102896 (closure operators), A102894 (strict closure operators), A000798 (topologies).
